-- a motion whose rate is still a function of the temperature. A Motion above is a motion at one
-- temperature, with its rate already a number; this is the motion itself, and the two are one layer
-- apart. Cyclohexane does not have two motion lists, one warm and one cold. It has one list, and the
-- temperature is an input to the count.
TempMotion : Type 0
TempMotion = (p : Nat → Nat) × ((r : Nat → Nat) × Bool)
